+**Windows compiler and cache safety.** The runtime and this tool accept only a
+GCC-compatible compiler that can produce a DLL for the runtime's PE architecture.
+When `gcc` is selected from `PATH`, candidates are checked rather than trusting
+the first executable name; Cygwin/MSYS targets are rejected. A configured
+`overlay_toolchain/compiler.txt` choice is preserved and produces a clear error
+if it is missing or incompatible. The emitted DLL is inspected before cache
+publication, and cached DLLs are checked before loading. Legacy DLLs with the
+wrong PE architecture or direct MSYS/Cygwin runtime imports are left on disk,
+ignored by the loader, and replaced atomically when a compatible rebuild is
+produced; caches are not cleared.
+
